IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `cbca-core`
IMPORT `cb2-nouns`

-- Canada Business Corporations Act (R.S.C. 1985, c. C-44), Part VIII, sections 82 to 93 -- TRUST INDENTURES:
-- the definitions, when the Part applies, the trustee's conflict of interest and qualification, the list of
-- security holders, evidence of compliance, notice of default, and the trustee's duty of care. Layer 1.
--
-- UNOFFICIAL. Encoded from a plain-text rendering of the Justice Canada consolidation current to
-- 2026-09-30, which is not an official version; nothing here is verified against the official text.
--
-- HOW TO READ A RULE. Named `<what it works out> within s <section>`. Where a provision says what follows in
-- a stated case, the rule is TRUE when that case holds; FALSE means only that this provision does not apply.
-- A rule whose result is a MAYBE returns NOTHING where the text is silent for the case.
-- A defined term of s 82(1) used to classify a person or an instrument ("trust indenture", "trustee", "event
-- of default") is a plain BOOLEAN input named for it, as in the other modules; the rule `<term> within s
-- 82(1)` is how a caller works it out. Any other rule that depends on a sibling in this module calls it and
-- takes its inputs. The Part applies only to a trust indenture within s 82(2) and not exempted under
-- s 82(3); no rule below asks that again, because the text of ss 83 to 93 does not.

§ `s 82 Definitions and application`

§§ `s 82(1) Definitions`

-- "trust indenture": any deed, indenture or other instrument or act, including any supplement or
-- amendment, made by a corporation after its incorporation or continuance under this Act, under which the
-- corporation issues debt obligations and in which a person is appointed as trustee for the holders. This is
-- also the term s 48(2) points to.
-- src:1097 | trust indenture means any deed, indenture or other instrument or act, including any supplement or amendment, made by a corporation after its incorporation or continuance under this Act, under which the corporation issues debt obligations and in which a person is appointed as trustee for the holders of the debt obligations. (acte de fiducie)
@ref CBCA s 82(1) "trust indenture" (src:1097)
GIVEN `the instrument is a deed, indenture or other instrument or act, including any supplement or amendment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it was made by a corporation after its incorporation or continuance under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `under it the corporation issues debt obligations` IS A BOOLEAN
      `in it a person is appointed as trustee for the holders of the debt obligations` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`trust indenture within s 82(1)` MEANS
        `the instrument is a deed, indenture or other instrument or act, including any supplement or amendment`
    AND `it was made by a corporation after its incorporation or continuance under this Act`
    AND `under it the corporation issues debt obligations`
    AND `in it a person is appointed as trustee for the holders of the debt obligations`

-- "trustee": any person appointed as trustee, including the administrator of the property of others, under
-- the terms of a trust indenture to which a corporation is a party, and any successor trustee. That the
-- appointee is an administrator of the property of others makes no difference, so no input asks.
-- src:1096 | trustee means any person appointed as trustee, including the administrator of the property of others, under the terms of a trust indenture to which a corporation is a party and includes any successor trustee; (fiduciaire)
@ref CBCA s 82(1) "trustee" (src:1096)
GIVEN `the person is appointed as trustee under the terms of a trust indenture to which a corporation is a party` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a successor trustee` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`trustee within s 82(1)` MEANS
        `the person is appointed as trustee under the terms of a trust indenture to which a corporation is a party`
    OR  `the person is a successor trustee`

-- "event of default": an event specified in a trust indenture on whose occurrence (a) a security interest
-- constituted by the indenture becomes enforceable or (b) the principal, interest and other moneys payable
-- become or may be declared payable before maturity; but it is not an event of default until all conditions
-- prescribed by the indenture for the giving of notice or the lapse of time or otherwise have been satisfied.
-- src:1092 | event of default means an event specified in a trust indenture on the occurrence of which
-- src:1093 | (a) a security interest constituted by the trust indenture becomes enforceable, or
-- src:1094 | (b) the principal, interest and other moneys payable thereunder become or may be declared to be payable before maturity,
-- src:1095 | but the event is not an event of default until all conditions prescribed by the trust indenture in connection with such event for the giving of notice or the lapse of time or otherwise have been satisfied; (cas de défaut)
@ref CBCA s 82(1) "event of default" (src:1092-1095)
GIVEN `the event is specified in a trust indenture` IS A BOOLEAN
      `on its occurrence a security interest constituted by the trust indenture becomes enforceable` IS A BOOLEAN
      `on its occurrence the principal, interest and other moneys payable become or may be declared to be payable before maturity` IS A BOOLEAN
      `all conditions prescribed by the trust indenture in connection with the event for the giving of notice or the lapse of time or otherwise have been satisfied` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`event of default within s 82(1)` MEANS
        `the event is specified in a trust indenture`
    AND (   `on its occurrence a security interest constituted by the trust indenture becomes enforceable`
         OR `on its occurrence the principal, interest and other moneys payable become or may be declared to be payable before maturity`)
    AND `all conditions prescribed by the trust indenture in connection with the event for the giving of notice or the lapse of time or otherwise have been satisfied`

§§ `s 82(2) Application`

-- src:1098 | Application
-- src:1099 | (2) This Part applies to a trust indenture if the debt obligations issued or to be issued under the trust indenture are part of a distribution to the public.
@ref CBCA s 82(2) (src:1098-1099)
GIVEN `the instrument is a trust indenture` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the debt obligations issued or to be issued under the trust indenture are part of a distribution to the public` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`this Part applies to the trust indenture within s 82(2)` MEANS
        `the instrument is a trust indenture`
    AND `the debt obligations issued or to be issued under the trust indenture are part of a distribution to the public`

§§ `s 82(3) Exemption`

-- The Director's power. The condition is the equivalence of a law of a province or another country; whether
-- the Director finds it so is the Director's judgement, so the input is the condition itself.
-- src:1100 | Exemption
-- src:1101 | (3) The Director may exempt a trust indenture from this Part if the trust indenture, the debt obligations issued thereunder and the security interest effected thereby are subject to a law of a province or a country other than Canada that is substantially equivalent to this Part.
@ref CBCA s 82(3) (src:1100-1101)
GIVEN `the trust indenture, the debt obligations issued thereunder and the security interest effected thereby are subject to a law of a province or a country other than Canada that is substantially equivalent to this Part` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the Director may exempt the trust indenture from this Part within s 82(3)` MEANS
    `the trust indenture, the debt obligations issued thereunder and the security interest effected thereby are subject to a law of a province or a country other than Canada that is substantially equivalent to this Part`

-- src:1098 | Application
-- src:1099 | (2) This Part applies to a trust indenture if the debt obligations issued or to be issued under the trust indenture are part of a distribution to the public.
-- src:1100 | Exemption
-- src:1101 | (3) The Director may exempt a trust indenture from this Part if the trust indenture, the debt obligations issued thereunder and the security interest effected thereby are subject to a law of a province or a country other than Canada that is substantially equivalent to this Part.
@ref CBCA s 82(2)-(3) (src:1098-1101)
GIVEN `the instrument is a trust indenture` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the debt obligations issued or to be issued under the trust indenture are part of a distribution to the public` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Director has exempted the trust indenture from this Part` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`this Part applies to the trust indenture after any exemption within s 82(3)` MEANS
        `this Part applies to the trust indenture within s 82(2)`
            `the instrument is a trust indenture`
            `the debt obligations issued or to be issued under the trust indenture are part of a distribution to the public`
    AND (NOT `the Director has exempted the trust indenture from this Part`)

§ `s 83 Conflict of interest`

§§ `s 83(1) Conflict of interest`

-- src:1102 | Conflict of interest
-- src:1103 | 83 (1) No person shall be appointed as trustee if there is a material conflict of interest between their role as trustee and their role in any other capacity.
@ref CBCA s 83(1) (src:1102-1103)
GIVEN `there is a material conflict of interest between the person's role as trustee and their role in any other capacity` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the person must not be appointed as trustee within s 83(1)` MEANS
    `there is a material conflict of interest between the person's role as trustee and their role in any other capacity`

§§ `s 83(2) Eliminating conflict of interest`

-- Within ninety days after becoming aware that a material conflict of interest exists, the trustee shall
-- eliminate it or resign. The core counts the day of becoming aware as the first day (fork F1).
-- src:1104 | Eliminating conflict of interest
-- src:1105 | (2) A trustee shall, within ninety days after becoming aware that a material conflict of interest exists
-- src:1106 | (a) eliminate such conflict of interest; or
-- src:1107 | (b) resign from office.
@ref CBCA s 83(2) (src:1104-1107)
GIVEN `the date the trustee became aware that a material conflict of interest exists` IS A DATE
      `the date the trustee eliminated the conflict of interest, if they did` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the date the trustee resigned from office, if they did` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the trustee has complied with the duty to eliminate the conflict or resign within s 83(2)` MEANS
        `acted in time` `the date the trustee eliminated the conflict of interest, if they did`
    OR  `acted in time` `the date the trustee resigned from office, if they did`
    WHERE
        `acted in time` act MEANS
            CONSIDER act
            WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
            WHEN JUST d THEN `done within the time limit` (`Time limit` WITH `number of units` IS 90, `unit of time` IS `calendar days`) `the date the trustee became aware that a material conflict of interest exists` d

-- src:1104 | Eliminating conflict of interest
-- src:1105 | (2) A trustee shall, within ninety days after becoming aware that a material conflict of interest exists
-- src:1106 | (a) eliminate such conflict of interest; or
-- src:1107 | (b) resign from office.
@ref CBCA s 83(2) (src:1104-1107)
GIVEN `the date the trustee became aware that a material conflict of interest exists` IS A DATE
      `the date the trustee eliminated the conflict of interest, if they did` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the date the trustee resigned from office, if they did` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the day asked about` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the trustee is in breach of the duty to eliminate the conflict or resign within s 83(2)` MEANS
        `the day asked about` GREATER THAN (`the last day of` (`Time limit` WITH `number of units` IS 90, `unit of time` IS `calendar days`) `counted from` `the date the trustee became aware that a material conflict of interest exists`)
    AND (NOT `the trustee has complied with the duty to eliminate the conflict or resign within s 83(2)`
                 `the date the trustee became aware that a material conflict of interest exists`
                 `the date the trustee eliminated the conflict of interest, if they did`
                 `the date the trustee resigned from office, if they did`)

§§ `s 83(3) Validity`

-- NOTHING: the trustee has no material conflict of interest, so s 83(3) says nothing.
-- src:1108 | Validity
-- src:1109 | (3) A trust indenture, any debt obligations issued thereunder and a security interest effected thereby are valid notwithstanding a material conflict of interest of the trustee.
@ref CBCA s 83(3) (src:1108-1109)
GIVEN `the trustee has a material conflict of interest` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the conflict invalidates the trust indenture, the debt obligations or the security interest within s 83(3)` MEANS
    IF `the trustee has a material conflict of interest`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `s 83(4) Removal of trustee`

-- src:1110 | Removal of trustee
-- src:1111 | (4) If a trustee contravenes subsection (1) or (2), any interested person may apply to a court for an order that the trustee be replaced, and the court may make an order on such terms as it thinks fit.
@ref CBCA s 83(4) (src:1110-1111)
GIVEN `the person was appointed as trustee although there was a material conflict of interest` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date the trustee became aware that a material conflict of interest exists` IS A DATE
      `the date the trustee eliminated the conflict of interest, if they did` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the date the trustee resigned from office, if they did` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the day asked about` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the trustee has contravened subsection 83(1) or (2) within s 83(4)` MEANS
        `the person was appointed as trustee although there was a material conflict of interest`
    OR  `the trustee is in breach of the duty to eliminate the conflict or resign within s 83(2)`
            `the date the trustee became aware that a material conflict of interest exists`
            `the date the trustee eliminated the conflict of interest, if they did`
            `the date the trustee resigned from office, if they did`
            `the day asked about`

-- src:1110 | Removal of trustee
-- src:1111 | (4) If a trustee contravenes subsection (1) or (2), any interested person may apply to a court for an order that the trustee be replaced, and the court may make an order on such terms as it thinks fit.
@ref CBCA s 83(4) (src:1110-1111)
GIVEN `the person was appointed as trustee although there was a material conflict of interest` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date the trustee became aware that a material conflict of interest exists` IS A DATE
      `the date the trustee eliminated the conflict of interest, if they did` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the date the trustee resigned from office, if they did` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the day asked about` IS A DATE
      `the applicant is an interested person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`an interested person may apply to a court for an order that the trustee be replaced within s 83(4)` MEANS
        `the applicant is an interested person`
    AND `the trustee has contravened subsection 83(1) or (2) within s 83(4)`
            `the person was appointed as trustee although there was a material conflict of interest`
            `the date the trustee became aware that a material conflict of interest exists`
            `the date the trustee eliminated the conflict of interest, if they did`
            `the date the trustee resigned from office, if they did`
            `the day asked about`

-- The court "may make an order on such terms as it thinks fit": its discretion over the terms is the court's.
-- src:1110 | Removal of trustee
-- src:1111 | (4) If a trustee contravenes subsection (1) or (2), any interested person may apply to a court for an order that the trustee be replaced, and the court may make an order on such terms as it thinks fit.
@ref CBCA s 83(4) (src:1110-1111)
GIVEN `the person was appointed as trustee although there was a material conflict of interest` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date the trustee became aware that a material conflict of interest exists` IS A DATE
      `the date the trustee eliminated the conflict of interest, if they did` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the date the trustee resigned from office, if they did` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the day asked about` IS A DATE
      `an interested person has applied to the court` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the court may make an order on such terms as it thinks fit within s 83(4)` MEANS
        `an interested person has applied to the court`
    AND `the trustee has contravened subsection 83(1) or (2) within s 83(4)`
            `the person was appointed as trustee although there was a material conflict of interest`
            `the date the trustee became aware that a material conflict of interest exists`
            `the date the trustee eliminated the conflict of interest, if they did`
            `the date the trustee resigned from office, if they did`
            `the day asked about`

§ `s 84 Qualification of trustee`

-- src:1112 | Qualification of trustee
-- src:1113 | 84 A trustee, or at least one of the trustees if more than one is appointed, shall be a body corporate incorporated under the laws of Canada or a province and authorized to carry on the business of a trust company.
@ref CBCA s 84 (src:1112-1113)
GIVEN `at least one of the trustees appointed is a body corporate incorporated under the laws of Canada or a province and authorized to carry on the business of a trust company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the requirement for a qualified trustee is met within s 84` MEANS
    `at least one of the trustees appointed is a body corporate incorporated under the laws of Canada or a province and authorized to carry on the business of a trust company`

§ `s 85 List of security holders`

§§ `s 85(4) Contents of statutory declaration`

-- src:1124 | Contents of statutory declaration
-- src:1125 | (4) The statutory declaration required under subsection (1) shall state
-- src:1126 | (a) the name and address of the person requiring the trustee to furnish the list and, if the person is a body corporate, the address for service thereof; and
-- src:1127 | (b) that the list will not be used except as permitted under subsection (5).
@ref CBCA s 85(4) (src:1124-1127)
GIVEN `the declaration states the name and address of the person requiring the trustee to furnish the list` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person requiring the list is a body corporate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the declaration states the address for service of the body corporate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the declaration states that the list will not be used except as permitted under subsection 85(5)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the statutory declaration states what it must within s 85(4)` MEANS
        `the declaration states the name and address of the person requiring the trustee to furnish the list`
    AND (   (NOT `the person requiring the list is a body corporate`)
         OR `the declaration states the address for service of the body corporate`)
    AND `the declaration states that the list will not be used except as permitted under subsection 85(5)`

§§ `s 85(3) Corporate applicant`

-- TRUE where the requirement is met or does not apply (the person requiring the list is not a body corporate).
-- src:1122 | Corporate applicant
-- src:1123 | (3) If the person requiring the trustee to furnish a list under subsection (1) is a body corporate, the statutory declaration required under that subsection shall be made by a director or officer of the body corporate.
@ref CBCA s 85(3) (src:1122-1123)
GIVEN `the person requiring the list is a body corporate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the statutory declaration is made by a director or officer of the body corporate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the statutory declaration is made by the right person within s 85(3)` MEANS
        (NOT `the person requiring the list is a body corporate`)
    OR  `the statutory declaration is made by a director or officer of the body corporate`

§§ `s 85(1) List of security holders`

-- The holder may require the list on payment of a reasonable fee, and the trustee must furnish it within
-- fifteen days after the holder delivers the statutory declaration. The duty arises when the holder has paid
-- the fee and has delivered a statutory declaration that meets ss 85(3) and (4).
-- src:1114 | List of security holders
-- src:1115 | 85 (1) A holder of debt obligations issued under a trust indenture may, on payment to the trustee of a reasonable fee, require the trustee to furnish, within fifteen days after delivering to the trustee the statutory declaration referred to in subsection (4), a list setting out
-- src:1116 | (a) the names and addresses of the registered holders of the outstanding debt obligations,
-- src:1117 | (b) the principal amount of outstanding debt obligations owned by each such holder, and
-- src:1118 | (c) the aggregate principal amount of debt obligations outstanding
-- src:1119 | as shown on the records maintained by the trustee on the day that the statutory declaration is delivered to that trustee.
@ref CBCA s 85(1) (src:1114-1119)
GIVEN `the person is a holder of debt obligations issued under a trust indenture` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the holder pays the trustee a reasonable fee` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the holder delivers a statutory declaration to the trustee` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the declaration states the name and address of the person requiring the trustee to furnish the list` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person requiring the list is a body corporate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the declaration states the address for service of the body corporate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the declaration states that the list will not be used except as permitted under subsection 85(5)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the statutory declaration is made by a director or officer of the body corporate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the trustee must furnish the list within s 85(1)` MEANS
        `the person is a holder of debt obligations issued under a trust indenture`
    AND `the holder pays the trustee a reasonable fee`
    AND `the holder delivers a statutory declaration to the trustee`
    AND `the statutory declaration states what it must within s 85(4)`
            `the declaration states the name and address of the person requiring the trustee to furnish the list`
            `the person requiring the list is a body corporate`
            `the declaration states the address for service of the body corporate`
            `the declaration states that the list will not be used except as permitted under subsection 85(5)`
    AND `the statutory declaration is made by the right person within s 85(3)`
            `the person requiring the list is a body corporate`
            `the statutory declaration is made by a director or officer of the body corporate`

-- src:1114 | List of security holders
-- src:1115 | 85 (1) A holder of debt obligations issued under a trust indenture may, on payment to the trustee of a reasonable fee, require the trustee to furnish, within fifteen days after delivering to the trustee the statutory declaration referred to in subsection (4), a list setting out
-- src:1116 | (a) the names and addresses of the registered holders of the outstanding debt obligations,
-- src:1117 | (b) the principal amount of outstanding debt obligations owned by each such holder, and
-- src:1118 | (c) the aggregate principal amount of debt obligations outstanding
-- src:1119 | as shown on the records maintained by the trustee on the day that the statutory declaration is delivered to that trustee.
@ref CBCA s 85(1) (src:1114-1119)
GIVEN `the date the holder delivers the statutory declaration to the trustee` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day for the trustee to furnish the list within s 85(1)` MEANS
    `the last day of` (`Time limit` WITH `number of units` IS 15, `unit of time` IS `calendar days`) `counted from` `the date the holder delivers the statutory declaration to the trustee`

-- src:1115 | 85 (1) A holder of debt obligations issued under a trust indenture may, on payment to the trustee of a reasonable fee, require the trustee to furnish, within fifteen days after delivering to the trustee the statutory declaration referred to in subsection (4), a list setting out
-- src:1116 | (a) the names and addresses of the registered holders of the outstanding debt obligations,
-- src:1117 | (b) the principal amount of outstanding debt obligations owned by each such holder, and
-- src:1118 | (c) the aggregate principal amount of debt obligations outstanding
-- src:1119 | as shown on the records maintained by the trustee on the day that the statutory declaration is delivered to that trustee.
@ref CBCA s 85(1) (src:1115-1119)
GIVEN `the list sets out the names and addresses of the registered holders of the outstanding debt obligations` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the list sets out the principal amount of outstanding debt obligations owned by each such holder` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the list sets out the aggregate principal amount of debt obligations outstanding` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the list is as shown on the records maintained by the trustee on the day the statutory declaration is delivered` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the list contains what it must within s 85(1)` MEANS
        `the list sets out the names and addresses of the registered holders of the outstanding debt obligations`
    AND `the list sets out the principal amount of outstanding debt obligations owned by each such holder`
    AND `the list sets out the aggregate principal amount of debt obligations outstanding`
    AND `the list is as shown on the records maintained by the trustee on the day the statutory declaration is delivered`

§§ `s 85(2) Duty of issuer`

-- src:1120 | Duty of issuer
-- src:1121 | (2) On the demand of a trustee, the issuer of debt obligations shall furnish the trustee with the information required to enable the trustee to comply with subsection (1).
@ref CBCA s 85(2) (src:1120-1121)
GIVEN `the trustee demands information` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the information is required to enable the trustee to comply with subsection 85(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the issuer must furnish the trustee with the information within s 85(2)` MEANS
        `the trustee demands information`
    AND `the information is required to enable the trustee to comply with subsection 85(1)`

§§ `s 85(5) Use of list`

-- NOTHING: the list was not obtained under s 85, so s 85(5) says nothing about its use.
-- src:1128 | Use of list
-- src:1129 | (5) A list obtained under this section shall not be used by any person except in connection with
-- src:1130 | (a) an effort to influence the voting of the holders of debt obligations;
-- src:1131 | (b) an offer to acquire debt obligations; or
-- src:1132 | (c) any other matter relating to the debt obligations or the affairs of the issuer or guarantor thereof.
@ref CBCA s 85(5) (src:1128-1132)
GIVEN `the list was obtained under section 85` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the use is in connection with an effort to influence the voting of the holders of debt obligations` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the use is in connection with an offer to acquire debt obligations` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the use is in connection with any other matter relating to the debt obligations or the affairs of the issuer or guarantor thereof` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the use of the list is permitted within s 85(5)` MEANS
    IF `the list was obtained under section 85`
    THEN JUST (   `the use is in connection with an effort to influence the voting of the holders of debt obligations`
               OR `the use is in connection with an offer to acquire debt obligations`
               OR `the use is in connection with any other matter relating to the debt obligations or the affairs of the issuer or guarantor thereof`)
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `s 85(6) Offence`

-- src:1133 | Offence
-- src:1134 | (6) A person who, without reasonable cause, contravenes subsection (5) is guilty of an offence and liable on summary conviction to a fine not exceeding five thousand dollars or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding six months or to both.
@ref CBCA s 85(6) (src:1133-1134)
DECLARE `Maximum penalty on summary conviction` HAS
    `fine in dollars` IS A NUMBER
    `imprisonment in months` IS A NUMBER

-- src:1133 | Offence
-- src:1134 | (6) A person who, without reasonable cause, contravenes subsection (5) is guilty of an offence and liable on summary conviction to a fine not exceeding five thousand dollars or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding six months or to both.
@ref CBCA s 85(6) (src:1133-1134)
GIVEN `the list was obtained under section 85` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the use is in connection with an effort to influence the voting of the holders of debt obligations` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the use is in connection with an offer to acquire debt obligations` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the use is in connection with any other matter relating to the debt obligations or the affairs of the issuer or guarantor thereof` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person acted without reasonable cause` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the person is guilty of an offence within s 85(6)` MEANS
        `the list was obtained under section 85`
    AND (NOT (   `the use is in connection with an effort to influence the voting of the holders of debt obligations`
              OR `the use is in connection with an offer to acquire debt obligations`
              OR `the use is in connection with any other matter relating to the debt obligations or the affairs of the issuer or guarantor thereof`))
    AND `the person acted without reasonable cause`

-- Liable on summary conviction to a fine not exceeding $5,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding
-- six months or to both. NOTHING: the person is not guilty of the offence.
-- src:1133 | Offence
-- src:1134 | (6) A person who, without reasonable cause, contravenes subsection (5) is guilty of an offence and liable on summary conviction to a fine not exceeding five thousand dollars or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding six months or to both.
@ref CBCA s 85(6) (src:1133-1134)
GIVEN `the list was obtained under section 85` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the use is in connection with an effort to influence the voting of the holders of debt obligations` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the use is in connection with an offer to acquire debt obligations` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the use is in connection with any other matter relating to the debt obligations or the affairs of the issuer or guarantor thereof` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person acted without reasonable cause` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `Maximum penalty on summary conviction`
`the most the person is liable to on summary conviction within s 85(6)` MEANS
    IF `the person is guilty of an offence within s 85(6)`
           `the list was obtained under section 85`
           `the use is in connection with an effort to influence the voting of the holders of debt obligations`
           `the use is in connection with an offer to acquire debt obligations`
           `the use is in connection with any other matter relating to the debt obligations or the affairs of the issuer or guarantor thereof`
           `the person acted without reasonable cause`
    THEN JUST (`Maximum penalty on summary conviction` WITH `fine in dollars` IS 5000, `imprisonment in months` IS 6)
    ELSE NOTHING

§ `s 86 Evidence of compliance`

§§ `s 86(1) Evidence of compliance`

-- src:1135 | Evidence of compliance
-- src:1136 | 86 (1) An issuer or a guarantor of debt obligations issued or to be issued under a trust indenture shall, before doing any act under paragraph (a), (b) or (c), furnish the trustee with evidence of compliance with the conditions in the trust indenture relating to
-- src:1137 | (a) the issue, certification and delivery of debt obligations under the trust indenture;
-- src:1138 | (b) the release or release and substitution of property subject to a security interest constituted by the trust indenture; or
-- src:1139 | (c) the satisfaction and discharge of the trust indenture.
@ref CBCA s 86(1) (src:1135-1139)
DECLARE `Kind of act under s 86(1)` IS ONE OF
    `the issue, certification and delivery of debt obligations under the trust indenture`
    `the release or release and substitution of property subject to a security interest constituted by the trust indenture`
    `the satisfaction and discharge of the trust indenture`
    `an act of none of these kinds under s 86(1)`

-- src:1135 | Evidence of compliance
-- src:1136 | 86 (1) An issuer or a guarantor of debt obligations issued or to be issued under a trust indenture shall, before doing any act under paragraph (a), (b) or (c), furnish the trustee with evidence of compliance with the conditions in the trust indenture relating to
-- src:1137 | (a) the issue, certification and delivery of debt obligations under the trust indenture;
-- src:1138 | (b) the release or release and substitution of property subject to a security interest constituted by the trust indenture; or
-- src:1139 | (c) the satisfaction and discharge of the trust indenture.
@ref CBCA s 86(1) (src:1135-1139)
GIVEN `the kind of act` IS A `Kind of act under s 86(1)`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the issuer or guarantor must furnish evidence of compliance before the act within s 86(1)` MEANS
    NOT (`the kind of act` EQUALS `an act of none of these kinds under s 86(1)`)

-- src:1135 | Evidence of compliance
-- src:1136 | 86 (1) An issuer or a guarantor of debt obligations issued or to be issued under a trust indenture shall, before doing any act under paragraph (a), (b) or (c), furnish the trustee with evidence of compliance with the conditions in the trust indenture relating to
-- src:1137 | (a) the issue, certification and delivery of debt obligations under the trust indenture;
-- src:1138 | (b) the release or release and substitution of property subject to a security interest constituted by the trust indenture; or
-- src:1139 | (c) the satisfaction and discharge of the trust indenture.
@ref CBCA s 86(1) (src:1135-1139)
GIVEN `the kind of act` IS A `Kind of act under s 86(1)`
      `the evidence of compliance was furnished to the trustee before the act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the issuer or guarantor has complied with s 86(1)` MEANS
        (NOT `the issuer or guarantor must furnish evidence of compliance before the act within s 86(1)` `the kind of act`)
    OR  `the evidence of compliance was furnished to the trustee before the act`

§§ `s 86(2) Duty of issuer or guarantor`

-- src:1140 | Duty of issuer or guarantor
-- src:1141 | (2) On the demand of a trustee, the issuer or guarantor of debt obligations issued or to be issued under a trust indenture shall furnish the trustee with evidence of compliance with the trust indenture by the issuer or guarantor in respect of any act to be done by the trustee at the request of the issuer or guarantor.
@ref CBCA s 86(2) (src:1140-1141)
GIVEN `the trustee demands evidence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the evidence is of compliance with the trust indenture by the issuer or guarantor in respect of an act to be done by the trustee at the request of the issuer or guarantor` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the issuer or guarantor must furnish the evidence on demand within s 86(2)` MEANS
        `the trustee demands evidence`
    AND `the evidence is of compliance with the trust indenture by the issuer or guarantor in respect of an act to be done by the trustee at the request of the issuer or guarantor`

§ `s 87 Contents of declaration, etc.`

-- src:1142 | Contents of declaration, etc.
-- src:1143 | 87 Evidence of compliance as required by section 86 shall consist of
-- src:1144 | (a) a statutory declaration or certificate made by a director or an officer of the issuer or guarantor stating that the conditions referred to in that section have been complied with; and
-- src:1145 | (b) where the trust indenture requires compliance with conditions that are subject to review
-- src:1146 | (i) by legal counsel, an opinion of legal counsel that such conditions have been complied with, and
-- src:1147 | (ii) by an auditor or accountant, an opinion or report of the auditor of the issuer or guarantor, or such other accountant as the trustee may select, that such conditions have been complied with.
@ref CBCA s 87 (src:1142-1147)
GIVEN `a statutory declaration or certificate made by a director or an officer of the issuer or guarantor states that the conditions referred to in section 86 have been complied with` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the trust indenture requires compliance with conditions that are subject to review by legal counsel` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an opinion of legal counsel that such conditions have been complied with is furnished` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the trust indenture requires compliance with conditions that are subject to review by an auditor or accountant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an opinion or report of the auditor of the issuer or guarantor, or of such other accountant as the trustee may select, that such conditions have been complied with is furnished` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the evidence of compliance consists of what it must within s 87` MEANS
        `a statutory declaration or certificate made by a director or an officer of the issuer or guarantor states that the conditions referred to in section 86 have been complied with`
    AND (   (NOT `the trust indenture requires compliance with conditions that are subject to review by legal counsel`)
         OR `an opinion of legal counsel that such conditions have been complied with is furnished`)
    AND (   (NOT `the trust indenture requires compliance with conditions that are subject to review by an auditor or accountant`)
         OR `an opinion or report of the auditor of the issuer or guarantor, or of such other accountant as the trustee may select, that such conditions have been complied with is furnished`)

§ `s 88 Further evidence of compliance`

-- src:1148 | Further evidence of compliance
-- src:1149 | 88 The evidence of compliance referred to in section 87 shall include a statement by the person giving the evidence
-- src:1150 | (a) declaring that they have read and understand the conditions of the trust indenture described in section 86;
-- src:1151 | (b) describing the nature and scope of the examination or investigation on which the certificate, statement or opinion is based; and
-- src:1152 | (c) declaring that they have made the examination or investigation that they believe necessary to enable them to make their statements or give their opinions.
@ref CBCA s 88 (src:1148-1152)
GIVEN `the statement declares that the person has read and understands the conditions of the trust indenture described in section 86` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the statement describes the nature and scope of the examination or investigation on which the certificate, statement or opinion is based` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the statement declares that the person has made the examination or investigation they believe necessary to enable them to make their statements or give their opinions` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the evidence of compliance includes the statement it must within s 88` MEANS
        `the statement declares that the person has read and understands the conditions of the trust indenture described in section 86`
    AND `the statement describes the nature and scope of the examination or investigation on which the certificate, statement or opinion is based`
    AND `the statement declares that the person has made the examination or investigation they believe necessary to enable them to make their statements or give their opinions`

§ `s 89 Trustee may require evidence of compliance`

§§ `s 89(1) Trustee may require evidence of compliance`

-- src:1153 | Trustee may require evidence of compliance
-- src:1154 | 89 (1) On the demand of a trustee, the issuer or guarantor of debt obligations issued under a trust indenture shall furnish the trustee with evidence in such form as the trustee may require as to compliance with any condition thereto relating to any action required or permitted to be taken by the issuer or guarantor under the trust indenture.
@ref CBCA s 89(1) (src:1153-1154)
GIVEN `the trustee demands evidence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the evidence is as to compliance with a condition relating to an action required or permitted to be taken by the issuer or guarantor under the trust indenture` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the issuer or guarantor must furnish evidence in the form the trustee may require within s 89(1)` MEANS
        `the trustee demands evidence`
    AND `the evidence is as to compliance with a condition relating to an action required or permitted to be taken by the issuer or guarantor under the trust indenture`

§§ `s 89(2) Certificate of compliance`

-- "At least once in each twelve month period beginning on the date of the trust indenture": the periods run
-- from the date of the indenture, one year at a time (fork F-P8-1). A period is complete once the day asked about is on or
-- after the day that starts the next one; every complete period must hold at least one certificate.
-- src:1155 | Certificate of compliance
-- src:1156 | (2) At least once in each twelve month period beginning on the date of the trust indenture and at any other time on the demand of a trustee, the issuer or guarantor of debt obligations issued under a trust indenture shall furnish the trustee with a certificate that the issuer or guarantor has complied with all requirements contained in the trust indenture that, if not complied with, would, with the giving of notice, lapse of time or otherwise, constitute an event of default, or, if there has been failure to so comply, giving particulars thereof.
@ref CBCA s 89(2) (src:1155-1156)
GIVEN `the date of the trust indenture` IS A DATE
      `the dates on which the issuer or guarantor furnished a certificate` IS A LIST OF DATE
      `the day asked about` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a certificate was furnished in each completed twelve month period within s 89(2)` MEANS
    `from period` 0
    WHERE
        `the start of period` k MEANS
            `the last day of` (`Time limit` WITH `number of units` IS k, `unit of time` IS `calendar years`) `counted from` `the date of the trust indenture`
        `from period` k MEANS
            IF `the day asked about` LESS THAN (`the start of period` (k PLUS 1))
            THEN TRUE
            ELSE     any (GIVEN d YIELD d AT LEAST (`the start of period` k) AND d LESS THAN (`the start of period` (k PLUS 1))) `the dates on which the issuer or guarantor furnished a certificate`
                 AND `from period` (k PLUS 1)

-- src:1155 | Certificate of compliance
-- src:1156 | (2) At least once in each twelve month period beginning on the date of the trust indenture and at any other time on the demand of a trustee, the issuer or guarantor of debt obligations issued under a trust indenture shall furnish the trustee with a certificate that the issuer or guarantor has complied with all requirements contained in the trust indenture that, if not complied with, would, with the giving of notice, lapse of time or otherwise, constitute an event of default, or, if there has been failure to so comply, giving particulars thereof.
@ref CBCA s 89(2) (src:1155-1156)
GIVEN `the trustee demands a certificate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the issuer or guarantor must furnish the certificate on demand within s 89(2)` MEANS
    `the trustee demands a certificate`

-- src:1155 | Certificate of compliance
-- src:1156 | (2) At least once in each twelve month period beginning on the date of the trust indenture and at any other time on the demand of a trustee, the issuer or guarantor of debt obligations issued under a trust indenture shall furnish the trustee with a certificate that the issuer or guarantor has complied with all requirements contained in the trust indenture that, if not complied with, would, with the giving of notice, lapse of time or otherwise, constitute an event of default, or, if there has been failure to so comply, giving particulars thereof.
@ref CBCA s 89(2) (src:1155-1156)
GIVEN `there has been a failure to comply with a requirement of the trust indenture that, if not complied with, would with notice, lapse of time or otherwise constitute an event of default` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the certificate states that the issuer or guarantor has complied with all such requirements` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the certificate gives particulars of the failure` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the certificate says what it must within s 89(2)` MEANS
    IF `there has been a failure to comply with a requirement of the trust indenture that, if not complied with, would with notice, lapse of time or otherwise constitute an event of default`
    THEN `the certificate gives particulars of the failure`
    ELSE `the certificate states that the issuer or guarantor has complied with all such requirements`

§ `s 90 Notice of default`

-- The trustee shall give the holders notice of every event of default arising under the indenture and
-- continuing when the notice is given, within thirty days after becoming aware of it, unless the trustee
-- reasonably believes it is in the holders' best interests to withhold the notice and so informs the issuer
-- and guarantor in writing.
-- src:1157 | Notice of default
-- src:1158 | 90 The trustee shall give to the holders of debt obligations issued under a trust indenture, within thirty days after the trustee becomes aware of the occurrence thereof, notice of every event of default arising under the trust indenture and continuing at the time the notice is given, unless the trustee reasonably believes that it is in the best interests of the holders of the debt obligations to withhold such notice and so informs the issuer and guarantor in writing.
@ref CBCA s 90 (src:1157-1158)
GIVEN `an event of default has arisen under the trust indenture` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the event of default is continuing at the time the notice is given` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the trustee reasonably believes that it is in the best interests of the holders to withhold the notice` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the trustee informs the issuer and guarantor in writing that it withholds the notice` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the trustee must give the holders notice of the event of default within s 90` MEANS
        `an event of default has arisen under the trust indenture`
    AND `the event of default is continuing at the time the notice is given`
    AND (NOT (    `the trustee reasonably believes that it is in the best interests of the holders to withhold the notice`
              AND `the trustee informs the issuer and guarantor in writing that it withholds the notice`))

-- src:1157 | Notice of default
-- src:1158 | 90 The trustee shall give to the holders of debt obligations issued under a trust indenture, within thirty days after the trustee becomes aware of the occurrence thereof, notice of every event of default arising under the trust indenture and continuing at the time the notice is given, unless the trustee reasonably believes that it is in the best interests of the holders of the debt obligations to withhold such notice and so informs the issuer and guarantor in writing.
@ref CBCA s 90 (src:1157-1158)
GIVEN `the date the trustee became aware of the occurrence of the event of default` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day for the trustee to give notice within s 90` MEANS
    `the last day of` (`Time limit` WITH `number of units` IS 30, `unit of time` IS `calendar days`) `counted from` `the date the trustee became aware of the occurrence of the event of default`

-- src:1157 | Notice of default
-- src:1158 | 90 The trustee shall give to the holders of debt obligations issued under a trust indenture, within thirty days after the trustee becomes aware of the occurrence thereof, notice of every event of default arising under the trust indenture and continuing at the time the notice is given, unless the trustee reasonably believes that it is in the best interests of the holders of the debt obligations to withhold such notice and so informs the issuer and guarantor in writing.
@ref CBCA s 90 (src:1157-1158)
GIVEN `an event of default has arisen under the trust indenture` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the event of default is continuing at the time the notice is given` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the trustee reasonably believes that it is in the best interests of the holders to withhold the notice` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the trustee informs the issuer and guarantor in writing that it withholds the notice` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date the trustee became aware of the occurrence of the event of default` IS A DATE
      `the date the trustee gave notice to the holders, if it did` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the day asked about` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the trustee is in breach of the duty to give notice of default within s 90` MEANS
        `the trustee must give the holders notice of the event of default within s 90`
            `an event of default has arisen under the trust indenture`
            `the event of default is continuing at the time the notice is given`
            `the trustee reasonably believes that it is in the best interests of the holders to withhold the notice`
            `the trustee informs the issuer and guarantor in writing that it withholds the notice`
    AND `the day asked about` GREATER THAN (`the last day for the trustee to give notice within s 90` `the date the trustee became aware of the occurrence of the event of default`)
    AND (NOT CONSIDER `the date the trustee gave notice to the holders, if it did`
             WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
             WHEN JUST d THEN `done within the time limit` (`Time limit` WITH `number of units` IS 30, `unit of time` IS `calendar days`) `the date the trustee became aware of the occurrence of the event of default` d)

§ `s 91 Duty of care`

-- src:1159 | Duty of care
-- src:1160 | 91 A trustee in exercising their powers and discharging their duties shall
-- src:1161 | (a) act honestly and in good faith with a view to the best interests of the holders of the debt obligations issued under the trust indenture; and
-- src:1162 | (b) exercise the care, diligence and skill of a reasonably prudent trustee.
@ref CBCA s 91 (src:1159-1162)
GIVEN `the trustee acts honestly and in good faith with a view to the best interests of the holders of the debt obligations issued under the trust indenture` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the trustee exercises the care, diligence and skill of a reasonably prudent trustee` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the trustee has discharged the duty of care within s 91` MEANS
        `the trustee acts honestly and in good faith with a view to the best interests of the holders of the debt obligations issued under the trust indenture`
    AND `the trustee exercises the care, diligence and skill of a reasonably prudent trustee`

§ `s 92 Reliance on statements`

-- src:1163 | Reliance on statements
-- src:1164 | 92 Notwithstanding section 91, a trustee is not liable if they rely in good faith on statements contained in a statutory declaration, certificate, opinion or report that complies with this Act or the trust indenture.
@ref CBCA s 92 (src:1163-1164)
GIVEN `the trustee relies in good faith on statements contained in a document` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the document is a statutory declaration, certificate, opinion or report` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the document complies with this Act or the trust indenture` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the trustee is not liable within s 92` MEANS
        `the trustee relies in good faith on statements contained in a document`
    AND `the document is a statutory declaration, certificate, opinion or report`
    AND `the document complies with this Act or the trust indenture`

§ `s 93 No exculpation`

-- A term that would relieve a trustee from the duties of s 91 does not operate to do so. NOTHING: the term is
-- not a term of one of the three kinds of document, or would not relieve the trustee, so s 93 says nothing.
-- src:1165 | No exculpation
-- src:1166 | 93 No term of a trust indenture or of any agreement between a trustee and the holders of debt obligations issued thereunder or between the trustee and the issuer or guarantor shall operate so as to relieve a trustee from the duties imposed on the trustee by section 91.
@ref CBCA s 93 (src:1165-1166)
GIVEN `the term is a term of a trust indenture, of an agreement between a trustee and the holders of debt obligations issued under it, or of an agreement between the trustee and the issuer or guarantor` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the term would relieve the trustee from the duties imposed on the trustee by section 91` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the term operates to relieve the trustee from the duties imposed by section 91 within s 93` MEANS
    IF     `the term is a term of a trust indenture, of an agreement between a trustee and the holders of debt obligations issued under it, or of an agreement between the trustee and the issuer or guarantor`
       AND `the term would relieve the trustee from the duties imposed on the trustee by section 91`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE NOTHING
